{"i":0,"start_s":0.07,"end_s":0.3,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"- The"}
{"i":1,"start_s":0.54,"end_s":7.96,"speaker":"SPEAKER_00","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Senator from Vermont. - Mr. President, you know Vermonters are frustrated. They're angry. They've seen the Congress"}
{"i":2,"start_s":7.96,"end_s":24.2,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"unwilling, and able to do its job, keep the government running. They've seen the fact that we've passed, we've passed the budgets, we've passed a continuing resolution here in the Senate. In a small group,"}
{"i":3,"start_s":24.14,"end_s":24.26,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"in"}
{"i":4,"start_s":24.41,"end_s":30.45,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"the House of Representatives, a small group of Republicans say, no, we have to have everything"}
{"i":5,"start_s":30.48,"end_s":30.83,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"we want"}
{"i":6,"start_s":31.25,"end_s":37.92,"speaker":"SPEAKER_00","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"or nothing. And that's why we see here in Washington, museums, national monuments barricaded."}
{"i":7,"start_s":38.16,"end_s":39.43,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"But it's more than just"}
{"i":8,"start_s":39.43,"end_s":43.68,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"that, Mr. President. This morning in the Judiciary Committee, we heard"}
{"i":9,"start_s":43.68,"end_s":44.38,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"from the"}
{"i":10,"start_s":44.38,"end_s":48.01,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Director of the National Security Agency that"}
{"i":11,"start_s":48.01,"end_s":51.86,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"as each day goes by, the impact and jeopardy of a shutdown"}
{"i":12,"start_s":51.84,"end_s":52.06,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"to"}
{"i":13,"start_s":52.38,"end_s":56.82,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"the safety and security of this country will increase."}
{"i":14,"start_s":56.84,"end_s":57.2,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"And"}
{"i":15,"start_s":57.43,"end_s":58.84,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"that's true."}
{"i":16,"start_s":58.84,"end_s":59.38,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"And the true"}
{"i":17,"start_s":59.43,"end_s":69.84,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"toll of this needless exercise is just beginning to be felt. Some decry federal spending as though it's some kind of a communicable disease. But millions of American families,"}
{"i":18,"start_s":70.43,"end_s":77.3,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Republicans, Democrats, Independents, rely on government-supported programs that provide the lifeline to keep them"}
{"i":19,"start_s":77.3,"end_s":77.94,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"going."}
{"i":20,"start_s":77.92,"end_s":78.29,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"key"}
{"i":21,"start_s":78.68,"end_s":84.55,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"nutrition programs, like the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program. My state that supports"}
{"i":22,"start_s":84.55,"end_s":105.9,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"100,000 Vermonters. Another 1,600 children and families benefit from Head Start. They're the ones that are gonna create, run our jobs in the next generation. More than 117,000 seniors are on Medicare, 200,000 Vermonters in Medicaid. They don't know how long this is gonna continue,"}
{"i":23,"start_s":106.17,"end_s":106.18,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"But"}
{"i":24,"start_s":106.25,"end_s":116.53,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"the shutdown is hurting in other areas, too. Buyers hoping to purchase a home with a loan from the Federal Housing Administration are being turned away. Can you imagine that ripple effect"}
{"i":25,"start_s":116.85,"end_s":117.45,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"when real estate"}
{"i":26,"start_s":117.52,"end_s":119.61,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"is finally starting to pick back up?"}
{"i":27,"start_s":119.67,"end_s":120.26,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"And what"}
{"i":28,"start_s":120.26,"end_s":125.77,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"they're saying is, oh, the economy, we worry about the economy. They're trying to kill the economy"}
{"i":29,"start_s":126.05,"end_s":126.48,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"by not"}
{"i":30,"start_s":126.48,"end_s":130.31,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"letting Federal Housing Administration work."}
{"i":31,"start_s":131.1,"end_s":131.32,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"In"}
{"i":32,"start_s":131.44,"end_s":144.86,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Vermont, 450 technicians of the National Guard were furloughed, just another hundred released from active orders. That financial effect, of course, but the national security effects are amazing."}
{"i":33,"start_s":144.86,"end_s":145.81,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"In Vermont,"}
{"i":34,"start_s":145.92,"end_s":158.56,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"we have a lot of agriculture. There's no one in the field or in the office at the Department of Agriculture. 200 USDA workers who, especially this time of year, are there to help Vermonters,"}
{"i":35,"start_s":158.78,"end_s":165.67,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"they've been forced to close up shop as a result of the shutdown. WIC, the Supplemental Food Program for Pregnant"}
{"i":36,"start_s":165.99,"end_s":166.49,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Women and"}
{"i":37,"start_s":166.53,"end_s":188.5,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Young Children, is 100% federally funded. But there's only two weeks of funding available in Vermont for the nearly 16,000 participants of the state. And we say in two weeks, \"Sorry, child,\" or \"Sorry, pregnant woman, we can't feed you.\" Can't just wait until we get our act together, but we're eating very well."}
{"i":38,"start_s":188.48,"end_s":192.02,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"We're eating very well, but could you go without food"}
{"i":39,"start_s":192.22,"end_s":192.27,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"for a"}
{"i":40,"start_s":192.29,"end_s":203.8,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"few weeks because we have a few more press conferences and a few more photo ops? What will happen to them? Our Republican colleagues in the House won't say. They apparently don't"}
{"i":41,"start_s":203.8,"end_s":204.59,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"care. We"}
{"i":42,"start_s":204.67,"end_s":211.98,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"heard from one office in Vermont, Rural Edge. They're building more affordable housing in St. Johnsbury, Vermont."}
{"i":43,"start_s":212.2,"end_s":212.88,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"The time has"}
{"i":44,"start_s":212.88,"end_s":215.56,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"come for them to pay the contractor."}
{"i":45,"start_s":215.81,"end_s":230.28,"speaker":"SPEAKER_05","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"The money is there, but nobody is at the USDA office to authorize the payment. Work is likely to stop. People have to be laid off. Winter is going to come, and that time to construct this affordable housing"}
{"i":46,"start_s":230.28,"end_s":231.15,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"is lost."}
